/* BARGE ESCAPE */
:: Arcology Stack Way Out
<<location "arcology_stack">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>><<set _bm to _st.bandMax or 10>><<set _rm to _st.routeMax or 5>>
You watch the drones travel between the sorting belts. Each one follows a particular path, and you begin looking for a time when you could cross the room without being seen.
<br><br>
The band around your ankle is locked, but you think a thin piece of scrap metal might loosen its hinge. You have also seen workers send discarded parts through an opening leading towards the sea door.
If you can remove the band and learn when the drones pass, that opening might give you a way out. Watching the patrols or working on the hinge takes half an hour.
<br><br>
<<if _st.band gt 0>>The band is <span class="teal"><<print Math.floor(_st.band * 100 / _bm)>>%</span> loose. <</if>><<if _st.route gt 0>>You have worked out <span class="teal"><<print _st.route>> of <<print _rm>></span> drone patrol routes.<</if>>
<<if _st.smuggler>><span class="green">Someone has prepared a place for you to hide among the scrap on the barge.</span><</if>>
<br><br>
<<set _stBandHint to !$daily.arcologyStackBand and _st.band lt _bm and _st.suspicion gt 40>>
<<set _stDarkHint to _st.band gte _bm and _st.route gte _rm and Time.hour gte 5 and Time.hour lt 22>>
<<set _stDoneHint to $daily.arcologyStackRoute and ($daily.arcologyStackBand or _st.band gte _bm) and !(_st.band gte _bm and _st.route gte _rm)>>
<<if _stBandHint>><span class="blue">The drones are checking your work area too often</span> for you to loosen the band safely. <</if>><<if _stDarkHint>><span class="blue">You can remove the band, and you know when the drones pass.</span> You need to wait until night to attempt your escape. <</if>><<if _stDoneHint>><span class="blue">You have already spent time preparing your escape today.</span> Doing more now could make the drones suspicious.<</if>>
<<if _stBandHint or _stDarkHint or _stDoneHint>><br><br><</if>>
<<if !$daily.arcologyStackRoute and _st.route lt _rm>>
	<<investigateicon>><<link [[Watch patrols (0:30)|Arcology Stack Patrols]]>><<set $daily.arcologyStackRoute to true>><<pass 30>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$daily.arcologyStackBand and _st.band lt _bm and _st.suspicion lte 40>>
	<<icon "mark.gif">><<link [[Loosen the band (0:30)|Arcology Stack Band]]>><<set $daily.arcologyStackBand to true>><<pass 30>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "skulduggery", 200, 900) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Skulduggery">>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if _st.band gte _bm and _st.route gte _rm and (Time.hour gte 22 or Time.hour lt 5)>>
	<<icon "prison-run.png">><<link [[Run|Arcology Stack Run]]>><<pass 3>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "skulduggery", 400, 1100) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Skulduggery">>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link `(!$daily.arcologyStackRoute && _st.route < _rm) || (!$daily.arcologyStackBand && _st.band < _bm && _st.suspicion <= 40) || (_st.band >= _bm && _st.route >= _rm && (Time.hour >= 22 || Time.hour < 5)) ? "Back to the bunks" : "Next"` "Arcology Stack Bunks">><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Patrols
<<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>><<set _rm to _st.routeMax or 5>>
<<set _st.route to Math.min(_rm, _st.route + 1)>>
You lie on a bunk facing the passage and keep your eyes partly closed whenever a drone moves past. From here, you can see the doorway without drawing attention to yourself.
<br><br>
You count how long it takes each drone to pass. The drones follow the same paths, but arrive at different times. After one passes the doorway, there are a few seconds before the next one appears.
<br><br>
You keep watching until you can remember which drone comes next and how long the passage stays clear.
<<if _st.route gte _rm>>
	<span class="green">You have learned the routes of every drone</span> between the bunks and the sea door, including the short gaps between patrols.
<<else>>
	You've worked out <span class="teal"><<print _st.route>> of <<print _rm>></span> patrol patterns.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Way Out]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Band
<<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>><<set _bm to _st.bandMax or 10>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<set _st.band to Math.min(_bm, _st.band + Math.max(setup.escapeAmount(), 0.5))>>
	You crouch beside a conveyor that has stopped moving. Its metal side blocks the nearest camera from seeing your ankle. You push a thin piece of scrap metal into the band's hinge, then press against the metal to loosen it.
	<br><br>
	When you hear a drone approaching, you stop working on the hinge and keep your hand beside your ankle until the drone passes.
	<br><br>
	<<if _st.band gte _bm>>
		<span class="green">The hinge is loose enough for you to open the band.</span> Its red numbers are still lit, so you leave it around your ankle until you are ready to escape.
	<<else>>
		The band is <span class="teal"><<print Math.floor(_st.band * 100 / _bm)>>%</span> loose.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You have barely pushed the piece of metal into the hinge when a drone comes around the conveyor. Its light moves towards your ankle, so you drop the scrap onto the floor and walk back to the bunks.
	<br><br>
	The drone follows you into the sleeping area. It passes your bunk several times, even after you lie down. <span class="red">You will have to be more careful while the drones are checking on you.</span> <<arcologyStackSuspicion 15>><<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Way Out]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Run
<<effects>>
Once the other workers are asleep, you return to your bunk and open the loosened band. You put it on your mattress, leaving its red numbers lit, then walk towards the sorting belts.
<br><br>
You remember the times you counted while watching the drones. Whenever one passes, you wait for the few seconds before the next patrol arrives.
<br><br>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You stay behind a metal support until the first drone passes. As soon as it turns the corner, you cross between two sorting belts and stop behind another piece of machinery.
	<br><br>
	A drone enters the next aisle before you can cross it. You crouch beneath a conveyor and watch its light move across the floor. Once the drone has passed, you crawl out and continue towards the sea door.
	<br><br>
	You reach the far end of the sorting room <span class="green">without setting off an alarm</span>.
	<br><br>
	A steep metal chute leads upwards to the sea door. Workers send old machinery through this opening to be collected outside. Oil covers parts of the chute, so climbing it will be difficult. The scrap barge should be nearby tonight.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Run 2]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "athletics", 400, 1000) ? "up" : "slip">><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You wait for a drone to pass before leaving your hiding place. Halfway to the next belt, another drone comes around the corner earlier than you expected.
	<br><br>
	You try to get behind the machinery, but <span class="red">the drone shines its light directly at you.</span> A siren sounds above the sorting room before you can reach cover.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Caught]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Stack Run 2
<<pass 2>><<effects>>
<<if $phase is "up">>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You get down on your hands and knees to climb the chute. The oil makes your feet slip, so you use the metal sides to support yourself as you move upwards.
	<br><br>
	Your hands are sore by the time you reach the top. The sea door is open, and cold air reaches you from outside. You look for the scrap barge, but it is farther behind the moving city, attached by a long rope.
	<br><br>
	Below you, seawater moves quickly through a narrow channel beneath the city. Large pumps take in water to help keep the floating city level, then release it near the back. You will have to swim through that channel to reach the barge.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Swim]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.stack.swim to { air: 3 }>><<water>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	As you climb, your foot slides across an oily patch of metal. You try to stop yourself by grabbing the sides of the chute, but you cannot find anything secure enough to hold.
	<br><br>
	You slide all the way to the bottom and hit the floor. A nearby drone turns towards the noise.<<pain 6>><<gpain>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Caught]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

/* UNDER THE HULL: the city is moving, so the barge trails on a tow line behind the stern. Each failed check costs a breath; none left means surfacing in a drone's light. */
:: Arcology Stack Swim
<<pass 1>><<effects>>
You drop into the cold water and go beneath the surface. The strong flow pushes you along the channel before you have time to choose where to swim. You hold your breath and try to keep your body away from the pipes and large metal covers around the pumps.
<br><br>
Small green work lights near the pipes help you see the machinery.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStackBreath>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Ride the current|Arcology Stack Swim Grate]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "swimming", 200, 900) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Swimming">>
<br>
<<link [[Grab the guide rail|Arcology Stack Swim Grate]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("force", "physique", 2000, 16000) ? 2 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Physique">>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Swim Grate
<<effects>>
<<set _ss to $xchange.arcology.stack.swim>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case 1>>
	You let the water carry you forwards and use small kicks to change direction. Whenever a pipe comes close, you turn your body to avoid it. <span class="green">You reach the end of the channel without hitting the machinery.</span>
<<case 2>>
	You grab the metal rail fixed along the channel wall. Keeping one hand on it, you reach forwards with the other and pull yourself towards the end of the channel. <span class="green">The rail lets you stay close to the wall while the water rushes past.</span>
<<default>>
	The moving water turns your body sideways, and you hit the metal covering of a pump. <span class="red">The impact makes you release some of the air you were holding,</span> and bubbles rise past your face. <<pain 8>><<gpain>><<set _ss.air-->>
<</switch>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<if _ss.air lte 0>>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Swim Surface]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	At the end of the channel, the strong flow pushes you against a large metal grate. You put your hands on its bars and try to keep your face away from the metal.
	<br><br>
	Through the grate, you can see the open water beneath the city. Two bars near the bottom have been bent apart, leaving a gap that might be wide enough for you to swim through.
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStackBreath>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Squeeze through the gap|Arcology Stack Swim Hull]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "athletics", 300, 1000) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Athletics">>
	<br>
	<<link [[Wait for the pumps to reverse|Arcology Stack Swim Hull]]>><<set $phase to 2>><<set _ss.air-->><<stress 6>><</link>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Swim Hull
<<effects>>
<<set _ss to $xchange.arcology.stack.swim>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case 1>>
	You turn sideways and put one arm through the gap, followed by the other. You pull your shoulders through and push with your feet until your hips fit between the bars. <span class="green">The metal scratches your skin, but you make it to the other side.</span> <<pain 4>><<gpain>>
<<case 2>>
	You keep both hands on the grate while the water pushes against your back. You badly need to breathe, but you wait for the pumps to change direction. When the flow becomes weaker, you pull yourself through the gap before the water starts pushing hard again.
<<default>>
	You manage to get your shoulders through the gap, but <span class="red">your clothes get caught on one of the bent bars.</span> You have to pull yourself backwards slightly to free the fabric before pushing through again. The struggle takes more of the air you were holding. <<pain 6>><<gpain>><<set _ss.air-->>
<</switch>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<if _ss.air lte 0>>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Swim Surface]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	After passing through the grate, you are swimming beneath the wide metal base of the city. A large metal fin, used to help keep the city steady, extends down into the water nearby. The water behind the engines is full of bubbles from the moving machinery.
	<br><br>
	A drone moves along the underside of the city. Its searchlight points into the water, moving from side to side as it looks for anyone swimming below.
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStackBreath>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Dive beneath the light|Arcology Stack Swim Wake]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "swimming", 300, 1000) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Swimming">>
	<br>
	<<link [[Hide in the fin's shadow|Arcology Stack Swim Wake]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "skulduggery", 300, 1000) ? 2 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Skulduggery">>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Swim Wake
<<effects>>
<<set _ss to $xchange.arcology.stack.swim>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case 1>>
	You swim deeper as the drone approaches. From below, you can see its searchlight moving across the water above you. <span class="green">The drone passes without seeing you.</span>
<<case 2>>
	You swim close to the large metal fin and put a hand against it to keep your position. The drone's searchlight moves across the nearby water, but the fin blocks the light from reaching you. <span class="green">The drone continues along the city without stopping.</span>
<<default>>
	The drone's searchlight reaches your arm. You pull it back beside your body and swim beneath the metal base, but <span class="red">the drone may have seen you.</span> Swimming so quickly makes it harder to keep holding your breath. <<set _ss.air-->><<arcologyStackSuspicion 10>>
<</switch>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
<<if _ss.air lte 0>>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Swim Surface]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You swim upwards through the water behind the city and finally reach the surface. You take several breaths while looking around for the scrap barge. The city is still moving forwards, with its illuminated dome visible above the water.
	<br><br>
	The barge is being pulled behind the city by a long rope. It is close enough to swim towards, but you are already falling behind. If you struggled underwater, you may not have enough strength left to catch it.
	<br><br>
	<<set _ssTired to (3 - _ss.air) * 150>>
	<<if $xchange.arcology.stack.smuggler>>
		<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Free]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "swimming", 100 + _ssTired, 800 + _ssTired) ? "hidden" : "sank">><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Free]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "swimming", 200 + _ssTired, 900 + _ssTired) ? "swam" : "sank">><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Swim Surface
<<effects>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
You cannot hold your breath any longer. You kick towards the surface as quickly as you can, then come out of the water coughing and trying to breathe.
<br><br>
Before you can swim away, a drone turns its searchlight towards you. The light stays on you, and a siren sounds from the city above.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Caught]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Free
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "hidden">>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You swim towards the blue mark on the scrap near the back of the barge. When you reach it, you grab the edge of the barge and pull yourself onto the pile of discarded metal.
	<br><br>
	Someone has cleared a space behind the marked block, large enough for you to hide inside. You crawl into it, then pull a loose metal plate across the opening so the crew cannot easily see you.
	<br><br>
	Nobody approaches your hiding place. The barge's engines start, and the barge begins moving away from the city.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Landing]]>><</link>>
<<elseif $phase is "swam">>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You swim towards the moving barge, trying to reach the long rope attached to its front. After several strokes, you manage to grab the rope and rest for a moment before pulling yourself along it.
	<br><br>
	You reach the side of the barge and climb over the edge, landing among broken mechanical arms and old cables.
	<br><br>
	<<if random(1, 100) lte 50>>
		You are still trying to catch your breath when you notice someone shining a torch across the scrap. <<arcologyNPC 0 "under" "loader">><<person1>>A <<person>> from the crew is walking between the piles of metal, checking the chains that keep everything in place.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Keep still|Arcology Stack Barge Found]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("run", "skulduggery", 300, 1000) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Skulduggery">>
		<br>
		<<link [[Jump the crew member first|Arcology Stack Barge Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		Nobody comes to check the scrap, so you stay hidden among it.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Landing]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You try to swim towards the barge, but the water moving behind the city's engines keeps pushing you backwards. The barge gets farther away, and your arms become too tired to keep up.
	<br><br>
	A drone flies out from the city and shines its light on the water around you. A siren sounds as the guards come to take you back.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Caught]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Barge Found
<<effects>>
<<person1>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You crouch beneath the old cables and keep your body still while the crew member checks the pile. The torch shines across a broken mechanical arm near your face, then moves away.
	<br><br>
	You wait until you hear the crew member walking towards the stairs. <span class="green">The <<person>> goes below deck without finding you.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Landing]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	The crew member shines the torch directly at your face. <span class="red">The <<person>> shouts for help,</span> then climbs over the scrap towards you before you can hide again.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Barge Fight
<<if $fightstart is 1>>
	<<set $fightstart to 0>>
	<<neutral 1>><<maninit>><<npcidlegenitals>>
	<<set $enemytrust -= 100>><<set $enemyanger += 200>>
<</if>>
<<set _scenePainMult to setup.arcology.fightPainMult()>><<set _scenePainFloor to setup.arcology.fightPainFloor()>>
<<effects>><<arcologyCombatNotes>><<effectsman>><<man>><<arcologyCyberTurn>><<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend or ($pain gte 100 and $willpowerpain is 0)>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Fight Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Fight]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Stack Barge Fight Finish
<<effects>>
<<if $enemyhealth lte 0 or $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>>
	<<if $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>><<ejaculation>><<else>><<run setup.arcology.noteWin()>><</if>>
	<<tearful>> you manage to push the <<person>> over the side of the barge. You quickly move to the other end and crawl beneath a pile of scrap before the rest of the crew arrives. The other crew members search the deck without finding you. The crew assumes the missing worker fell into the water.
	<br><br>
	<<clotheson>><<endcombat>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Barge Landing]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $finish is 1>><<encounterEndViolence>><</if>>
	Several crew members force you down against the pile of scrap and keep you there while one of them contacts the city. The barge begins turning back towards Arcology. <<tearful>> you watch the sky above the deck, knowing the drones will soon arrive.
	<br><br>
	<<clotheson>><<endcombat>>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Caught]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Barge Landing
<<pass `setup.arcology.voyageHours() * 60`>><<effects>>
<<badEndTrackingEnd "Arcology Stack" { reason: "arcologyStackRan" }>>
You spend several days hidden among the scrap. Your clothes gradually dry, but you have no blanket to keep out the wind. You sleep in short stretches, waking whenever the engines change pitch or footsteps pass your hiding place. Each time someone comes near, you crouch behind the scrap and wait for them to leave.
<br><br>
Eventually, the barge reaches the town docks. You wait until the barge stops beside the pier, then climb down onto it before the crew comes up from below deck.
<br><br>
The implant behind your ear is still active. Red text appears at the edge of your vision, reminding you that Arcology still considers you to be in debt.
<br><br>
<<set _holoMsg to "ABSCONDED. OUTSTANDING DEBT " + setup.arcology.cxU($xchange.arcology.stack.debt) + ".">>
<<holoNotice "CIVIC REGISTRY" _holoMsg "denied">>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Docks]]>><<set $xchange.arcology.debt to { amount: $xchange.arcology.stack.debt, runs: ($xchange.arcology.stack.runs or 0) + 1 }>><<arcologyStackEnd>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Caught
<<location "arcology_stack">><<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>>
<<set _st.band to 0>><<set _st.route to Math.min(_st.route, 2)>><<set _st.suspicion to 100>><<set _st.smuggler to false>><<run delete _st.swim>>
<<endevent>><<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "guard">><<person1>>
Guards in grey armour take hold of your arms and bring you back to the bunks. One guard checks your ankle, then locks a replacement band around your leg. The new hinge is positioned where you cannot reach it easily.
<br><br>
The guard shows you a new patrol schedule on a wrist screen. An extra drone has been assigned to watch you, changing the routes you memorised. <<arcologyStackCharge 2500>> <<stress 10>><<ggstress>><<trauma 4>><<gtrauma>>
<br><br>
"You still have to answer for trying to escape," the <<person>> says. The guard takes you by the arm and leads you away from the bunks.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Punishment]]>><</link>>
<br>

/* REVOLT */
:: Arcology Stack Revolt
<<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>>
<<set _sdCount to $phase>>
You climb onto a bunk and tap the nearby drone cable three times, giving the signal you agreed on with the other workers. You wait, watching the drones above the sorting belts.
<br><br>
The relay broadcasts your signal to the modified chips, including a command to erase the workers' debt records. A moment later, the drones' red camera lights turn white. The drones stop moving along their patrol routes and remain above the belts. Workers begin leaving the bunks and running towards the main passage.
<br><br>
<<if _sdCount gte 3>>
	The lights in the working area go out while smoke and the bright light from a flare appear near the sea door. At the same time, the guards' screens show an empty sorting room instead of the workers leaving their bunks.
	<br><br>
	The guards hurry towards different parts of the Stack to investigate. <span class="green">Nobody is left blocking your path to the service lift.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Victory]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _sdCount is 2>>
	<<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "security guard">><<person1>>
	The problems you arranged draw most of the guards away. <span class="blue">One security guard remains in front of the lift,</span> holding a weapon towards the approaching workers. <<arcologyCyberLook 0>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<<elseif _sdCount is 1>>
	<<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "security guard">><<arcologyNPC 1 "staff" "guard">><<arcologyNPC 2 "staff" "guard">><<person1>>
	Some guards leave to investigate the distraction you prepared. <span class="purple">Three guards remain in the corridor to the lift,</span> standing between you and the exit.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Fight]]>><<set $fightstart to 1>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "security guard">><<person1>>
	The drones have stopped patrolling, but the guards can still see the workers running towards the lift. Several guards step into the corridor and draw their batons.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">The workers at the front turn back when the guards begin hitting them,</span> forcing the people behind to stop as well.
	<br><br>
	You try to keep moving, but a <<person>> catches you by the collar before you reach the lift. <<arcologyStackCrew -10>><<set _st.net to Math.max(0, _st.net - 5)>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Punishment]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Revolt Fight
<<if $fightstart is 1>>
	<<set $fightstart to 0>>
	<<set $enemyno to $phase>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	<<neutral 1>><<maninit>><<npcidlegenitals>>
	<<set $enemytrust -= 100>><<set $enemyanger += 200>>
	<<person1>>
<</if>>
<<set _scenePainMult to setup.arcology.fightPainMult()>><<set _scenePainFloor to setup.arcology.fightPainFloor()>>
<<effects>><<arcologyCombatNotes>><<effectsman>><<man>><<arcologyCyberTurn>><<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend or ($pain gte 100 and $willpowerpain is 0)>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Fight Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Fight]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

