:: Arcology Stack Revolt Victory
<<effects>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>>
You reach the service lift, followed by the workers who escaped the guards. The lift doors are closed, and the control panel beside them shows a red warning light.
<br><br>
<<if _st.revolt.code>>
	<<pass 4>>
	You remember hearing the supervisors discuss the access code through a vent. You enter the shift number in reverse order, pressing one button at a time. <span class="green">The warning light turns green, and the lift doors unlock.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Free]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You do not know the code to open the lift. When you look above the closed doors, you see a maintenance hatch that leads into the space where the lift moves between floors.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Shaft]]>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "athletics", 400, 1100) ? 1 : 0>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Revolt Shaft
<<pass 10>><<effects>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	You pull yourself through the hatch and find a metal ladder fixed to the wall. You begin climbing, followed by the other workers. There is little room to move, so you keep climbing without stopping while more people come through the hatch below.
	<br><br>
	When you reach the pier level, your arms hurt from the climb. You find a lever beside the doors and pull it. The doors open, allowing everyone to leave the shaft.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Revolt Free]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $phase to 0>>
	Halfway up the ladder, your hand slips from a greasy step. You try to grab the next one, but fall backwards into the workers climbing below you. Several workers lose their hold, and you fall together to the bottom of the shaft. <<pain 15>><<ggpain>>
	<br><br>
	The drones begin patrolling again before you can climb out. By the time guards reach the hatch, you are still at the bottom of the shaft. <<arcologyStackCrew -10>>
	<br><br>
	<<endevent>><<arcologyNPC 0 "staff" "guard">><<person1>>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Punishment]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Revolt Free
<<pass 1>><<effects>>
<<badEndTrackingEnd "Arcology Stack" { reason: "arcologyStackRevolt" }>>
<<run setup.arcology.expose(5)>>
The doors open onto the pier, and the workers run outside. Some head along the waterfront while others take the stairs towards the lower streets. A few stop beside the exit, looking back at the dome above the city.
<br><br>
The warning in your implant disappears, then returns with letters and numbers you cannot make sense of.
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / STATUS CHANGE" "ok">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "STATUS" "RECORD CORRUPTED">>
	<<holoLine "DEBT NOT FOUND" "ok">>
<</holo>>
<br>
The Stack's debt records have been deleted during the revolt. Your implant no longer shows the amount you owed. You can leave the Stack, but <span class="red">the island's guards will soon be looking for the workers who escaped, including you.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Pier]]>><<arcologyStackEnd>><</link>>
<br>

/* The Stack's punishments, the island's answer to the mine's pit: the isolation pod, implant reconditioning, the compactor hold
   and a night sold to a buyer. Callers leave a guard in slot 0; every branch ends in <<arcologyStackPunishEnd>>. */
:: Arcology Stack Punishment
<<effects>><<person1>>
<<set _st to $xchange.arcology.stack>>
<<set _spPool to ["Pod", "Recondition", "Compactor"]>>
<<if _st.buyerSeen>><<set _spPool.push("Buyer", "Buyer")>><</if>>
<<set _spPick to _spPool.random()>>
The <<person>> takes you past the sleeping area and into a corridor away from the sorting belts. As you walk, the guard checks your record on a tablet and reads out the rule you broke. <<He>> keeps hold of your arm while leading you farther into the building.
<br><br>
<<set _spLink to "Arcology Stack " + _spPick>>
<<link [[Next|_spLink]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Pod
<<effects>><<person1>>
The corridor ends beside a row of narrow metal pods. Each is just large enough for someone to stand inside, with a small window near the top. The <<person>> opens one of the doors and pushes you inside before closing it. <<pain 4>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
The light switches off, leaving you in darkness. The walls block almost all the noise from the rest of the Stack. You move one foot against the floor, but even that makes very little sound. <<ggstress>><<stress 10>>
<br><br>
You try to count how much time has passed, but you cannot tell whether you have been inside for a few minutes or much longer. You feel the band around your ankle and start thinking about how many more shifts you will have to work. <<gggstress>><<stress 40>>
<br><br>
You remember the town across the water. You wonder whether anyone has looked for you since you disappeared, and whether you will be able to return. <<gggtrauma>><<trauma 300>>
<br><br>
<<link `$trauma >= 2500 ? "Wait (2:00)" : "Next"` "Arcology Stack Pod End">><</link>>
<br>
<<if $trauma gte 2500>>
	<<link [[Cry|Arcology Stack Pod Cry]]>><<trauma -50>><</link>><<llltrauma>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Stack Pod Cry
<<effects>>
<span class="red">You begin crying and cannot stop.</span> You cover your face with your hands, but there is nobody inside the pod to see you. Your cries sound faint through the walls, and no guard comes to check on you. <<ggstress>><<stress 10>>
<br><br>
After a while, you wipe your face and manage to stop crying. You lean against the wall and try to breathe normally again. <<trauma -25>><<llltrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Pod End]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Pod End
<<pass 2 hours>><<effects>><<person1>>
The door opens, letting the bright corridor lights shine inside. You close your eyes briefly before the <<person>> grabs your arm and pulls you out.
<br><br>
You stumble as you leave the pod, then manage to stand while the guard waits beside you.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStackPunishEnd>>

:: Arcology Stack Recondition
<<effects>><<person1>>
The <<person>> sits you in a chair bolted to the floor and straps your wrists to its arms. A technician wheels a console over and plugs a cable into the light behind your ear.
<br><br>
<<holo "IMPLANT / RECONDITIONING" "denied">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "PROGRAMME" "COMPLIANCE 3">>
	<<holoLine "USER CONSENT" "denied">>
<</holo>>
<br>
A sharp pain starts near the implant behind your ear and spreads through your head. Your vision fills with flashing lines, followed by large red words: <span class="red">STATION. SORT. COMPLY.</span>
<br><br>
You try to look away, but the instructions remain in front of your eyes. Another pulse makes your fingers move against the straps, as though you were already working at a sorting belt. <<pain 10>><<ggpain>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Fight it|Arcology Stack Recondition 2]]>><<pass 30>><<set $phase to setup.arcology.escape("stack", "willpower", 200, 1000) ? 1 : 0>><</link>><<arcologySkill "Willpower">>
<br>
<<link [[Let it run|Arcology Stack Recondition 2]]>><<pass 30>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Recondition 2
<<effects>>
<<switch $phase>>
<<case 1>>
	You repeat your own handle out loud to remind yourself who you are. The programme keeps showing the same orders, but you concentrate on saying your handle rather than following them.
	<br><br>
	After several more pulses, the same instruction stays on the display without changing. <span class="green">The programme stops, and the technician cannot make it continue.</span> The technician swears and presses several buttons on the console. <<willpower 3>><<gwillpower>><<stress 10>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	"You wouldn't follow the instructions," the technician says. The technician looks at the frozen display. "Put down that the treatment is complete. I'm not starting it again."
<<case 0>>
	You try to remember your own handle while the machine repeats its instructions. Each new pulse makes it harder to concentrate, until <span class="red">you begin repeating the sorting orders without meaning to.</span> You keep thinking about where each piece of scrap belongs, even though you are still strapped to the chair. <<trauma 30>><<ggtrauma>><<stress 20>><<ggstress>><<pain 10>><<ggpain>>
<<default>>
	You stop trying to resist the repeated instructions. As the machine continues, the pain begins to fade and a strange warmth spreads through your body. You stop pulling against the straps and listen to the orders instead. <<trauma 20>><<ggtrauma>><<arousal 1500>><<garousal>>
	<br><br>
	When the technician unplugs the cable, you find yourself waiting for another instruction to appear.
<</switch>>
<<set $phase to 0>>
<br><br>
The <<person>> removes the straps from your wrists. Your vision is still disturbed by small flashes of light as you get up from the chair.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStackPunishEnd>>

:: Arcology Stack Compactor
<<effects>><<person1>>
<<set _scPool to ["Empty"]>>
<<if $settings.tentaclesEnabled>><<set _scPool.push("Tendrils")>><</if>>
<<if $settings.slimesEnabled>><<set _scPool.push("Culture")>><</if>>
<<set _scPick to _scPool.random()>>
The <<person>> stops at a heavy metal door marked COMPACTOR HOLD / ORGANIC WASTE. The guard turns the wheel until the door opens, then pushes you inside.
<br><br>
You fall onto a floor that slopes down towards the drains. Something warm and slippery covers the metal beneath your hands. <<pain 5>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
The door closes above you, leaving you inside the room. A row of small green lights along one wall lets you see part of the floor. <<ggstress>><<stress 10>>
<br><br>
<<if _scPick is "Tendrils">>
	You see something moving behind the metal covers over the drains. The Stack uses living organisms to break down waste mixed in with the scrap, and some have been left inside this room.
	<br><br>
	Pale tendrils push through the openings and move across the floor towards you. <span class="red">One reaches your ankle while more emerge from the drains.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Compactor Tendrils]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _scPick is "Culture">>
	You try to get up, but the warm substance on the floor sticks to your hands. It is a living cleaning substance used to break down waste from the sorting belts.
	<br><br>
	As you move your hands away, the substance moves towards your legs. <span class="red">It gathers around your knees and slowly moves up your thighs.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Compactor Culture]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	There is nobody else inside the room. Machinery starts working somewhere above you, and the metal walls shake every few minutes. You move away from the walls each time, expecting the machine to start pushing them together.
	<br><br>
	The walls do not move any closer, but you keep looking up whenever the machinery starts again. <<gggstress>><<stress 30>><<trauma 100>><<ggtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Compactor End]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

